    seeing:
      "The Kyzylkum Desert occupies north-central Uzbekistan between the Amu Darya and the Syr Darya, its name meaning red sand. This entry covers the part within Uzbekistan. The desert slopes as a whole to the north-west, from about 300 m above sea level in the south-east to about 53 m in the north-west, and receives only 100 to 200 mm of rain a year.",
